message: "If you use this software or its results, please cite it as below."
title: "CTI RAG Poisoning Benchmark"
type: software
version: "1.3.2"
date-released: "2026-11-11"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/mpysiek/Projekt_RAG"
authors:
  - family-names: "Pyśk"
    given-names: "Mateusz"
    affiliation: "Military University of Technology (Wojskowa Akademia Techniczna), Faculty of Cybernetics, Warsaw, Poland"
abstract: >-
  Deterministic, zero-cost benchmark of retrieval-layer robustness to corpus poisoning in
  cyber threat intelligence (CTI) retrieval-augmented generation. Four retrieval
  architectures (BM25, dense bi-encoder, hybrid fusion with cross-encoder reranking,
  entity-graph traversal), a 24,000-document corpus from MITRE ATT&CK, CTIBench, CISA KEV
  and the CVE Program, 150 queries in three strata, nine attack vectors and budgets of one
  to five payloads.
keywords:
  - retrieval-augmented generation
  - corpus poisoning
  - cyber threat intelligence
  - retrieval robustness
  - graph-based retrieval
  - benchmark methodology
  - MITRE ATT&CK
preferred-citation:
  type: article
  title: "Rank Placement Is Not Displacement: A Deterministic Benchmark of Retrieval-Layer Robustness to Corpus Poisoning in Cyber Threat Intelligence RAG"
